# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  mcp-secrets.env  —  TEMPLATE  (copy, fill in, keep OUT of git)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  The tokens file for your IDE's / agent CLI's MCP servers (Jira, Confluence,
#  Bitbucket) — used by setup/mcp.cursor.json.template ("envFile") and
#  setup/mcp-with-secrets.sh.template. It is OPTIONAL.
#
#  THE BOARD ITSELF DOES NOT READ THIS FILE. The board reads only setup/.env,
#  which you fill from the board's API keys dialog (the key button in the header);
#  it is git-ignored, docker-ignored and never served.
#
#  WHERE TO PUT THE REAL FILE
#    Default location expected by the MCP templates:  ~/.cursor/mcp-secrets.env
#    (the MCP wrapper PARSES it line by line — nothing in it is executed.)
#     You can point elsewhere with the MCP_SECRETS_FILE env var.
#
#  HOW TO CREATE IT
#    cp setup/mcp-secrets.env.template ~/.cursor/mcp-secrets.env
#    chmod 600 ~/.cursor/mcp-secrets.env      # readable only by you
#    # then edit ~/.cursor/mcp-secrets.env and paste your real tokens
#
#  FORMAT: plain KEY=VALUE, one per line. No quotes needed. No spaces around =.
#  Lines starting with # are comments; an optional leading "export " and one layer
#  of surrounding quotes are accepted. Values are literal: $VAR, $(...) and
#  backticks are NOT expanded (the file is parsed, never sourced).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── REQUIRED: Jira ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of your Jira (no trailing slash). Data Center / Server, not cloud.
JIRA_URL=https://jira.your-company.example
# Personal Access Token (Jira → Profile → Personal Access Tokens → Create token).
JIRA_PERSONAL_TOKEN=replace-with-your-jira-PAT

# ── OPTIONAL: Confluence (enriches ticket briefs with linked docs) ────────────
CONFLUENCE_URL=https://confluence.your-company.example
CONFLUENCE_PERSONAL_TOKEN=replace-with-your-confluence-PAT

# ── OPTIONAL: Bitbucket (adds real branches + PR state to cards) ──────────────
# Bitbucket → Personal settings → HTTP access tokens. Read scope is enough.
BITBUCKET_PAT=replace-with-your-bitbucket-PAT

# ── OPTIONAL: Atlassian token (Bitbucket alternative) ────────────────────────
# The board's Bitbucket calls use ATLASSIAN_TOKEN only when BITBUCKET_PAT is unset
# (a fallback for BITBUCKET_PAT, not for JIRA_PERSONAL_TOKEN).
# ATLASSIAN_TOKEN=replace-with-your-atlassian-api-token

# ── OPTIONAL: connector CLI key (agent fallback only) ─────────────────────────
# The deterministic Python fetch is the primary path and needs no LLM key, so you
# do NOT need this to deploy. The board's agent fallback reads it from setup/.env
# (API keys dialog); keep a copy here only if your own agent CLI reads this file.
# The one matching connector.active in config/jira-board.config.json:
#   cursor  → CURSOR_API_KEY       (default)
#   claude  → ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#   codex   → OPENAI_API_KEY
# CURSOR_API_KEY=replace-with-your-cursor-api-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Your real machine may keep MANY more keys in this one file (Jenkins,
#  Dynatrace, JFrog, databases, …) for other tools. jira-board never reads it —
#  its own keys live in setup/.env. Keep this file out of the repo.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
